      "code": "ALTER TABLE Student",
      "explanation": "The ALTER TABLE statement can be used to drop one or more columns from an existing table. Note that dropping a column can pose the data-integrity issues. For example, if you drop a column that is a primary key in some relationship, the foreign key columns that refer to the dropped column become invalid."
